<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ayodhya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ayodhya is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarayu-river">Sarayu River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, revered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindus</a> as the birthplace and capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a>. Associated with the ancient kingdom of Kosala and the nearby city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saketa">Saketa</a>, it is also sacred to Jains as the birthplace of several tirthankaras. A long dispute over the Babri Mosque, demolished in 1992, ended with a Supreme Court ruling in 2019, and a Ram temple opened there in 2024.</p></div>
